<article class="env-definition" id="00SL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00SL">Definition <span data-tag="00SL">10.136.1</span>.</a> A ring map $R \to S$ is called <em>syntomic</em>, or we say $S$ is a <em>flat local complete intersection over $R$</em> if it is flat, of finite presentation, and if all of its fibre rings $S \otimes _ R \kappa (\mathfrak p)$ are local complete intersections, see Definition <a href="/tag/00S9" data-tag="00S9">10.135.1</a>. </p>
</article>